   "stem": {
      "text": "The integral test is applied to the series \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n^{2}+3} \\). Take f(x) to be the series' general term with n replaced by x, and the lower limit of integration to be the series' starting index. Find the exact value of the improper integral of f from that lower limit to infinity."
   },
   "answer_key": {
